## Tests policy

- Use **pytest** only.
- Use **freezegun** for time-based logic (cooldowns/debounce).
- Mock iRacing (`pyirsdk` / shared memory) and OBS client: **never use real connections** in tests.
- Prefer testing `logic/` independently of IO layers.
- Tests that bind the real HTTP port (`17321`) **fail if irswitch is already running**. That is an occupied-port environment issue, not a regression of the change under test. Stop the service, use another port in the test, or skip that case — do not “fix” production code to make the collision pass.

## What to test (priority)

- state machine transitions
- policy decisions (scene selection) including reasons
- cooldown/debounce behavior (monotonic time assumptions)
- error handling around external failures (no crash)

